      "title": "Trades requests count and return rows for filtered markets",
      "description": "The trades route reports `tape_filtered` based on the market\u2019s category, but `count_trades` and `fetch_trades` query `kalshi.trades` by ticker and time only. They do not apply the collection filter. If a market has stored trades and its category is excluded, the response still returns those trades instead of representing the tape as filtered; this also makes `count` inconsistent with the reported `tape_filtered` fact. Apply the same category exclusion to both count and fetch, or otherwise define and test why already-stored trades should remain visible.",
